hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17664","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: I heard 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id narrating, from Anas ibn Abi Anas, from 'Abd Allah ibn Nafi' Ibn al-'Amya', from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Prayer is two by two, and you make tashahhud in every two rak'ahs, show humility and neediness, raise your hand, and say: O Allah, O Allah. Whoever does not do that, it is deficient. And Hajjaj said: And you raise your hands."
"17665","Hajjaj narrated to us, who said: I heard Shu'bah, who said: I heard 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id narrating, from Anas ibn Abi Anas, from the people of Egypt, from 'Abd Allah ibn Nafi' Ibn al-'Amya', from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Prayer is two by two, and he mentioned the like of it."
"17666","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me, from 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id, from 'Imran, from 'Abd Allah, from Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Prayer is two by two; you make tashahhud in every two rak'ahs, humble yourself, show awe, be still, then raise your hands, saying: You raise them to your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, facing your face with their palms, and you say: O Lord, O Lord, three times. Whoever does not do that, it is deficient. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: This in my view is the correct one."
"17667","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yazid ibn 'Iyad informed us, from 'Imran ibn Abi Anas, from 'Abd Allah ibn Nafi' ibn Abi al-'Amya', from al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two, and when one of you prays, let him make tashahhud in every two rak'ahs, then let him be earnest in asking. Then when he supplicates, let him be still, humble, and lowly. Whoever does not do that, then that is deficient, or like deficient."
"17668","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shu'bah informed me, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Amr ibn Aws, from a man who narrated to him, the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The crier of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called on a rainy day: Indeed pray in your dwellings."
"17669","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, who said: Shu'bah informed me, from 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id, from 'Imran ibn Abi Anas, from the people of Egypt, from 'Abd Allah ibn Nafi', from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is two by two, and you make tashahhud and taslim in every two rak'ahs, show humility and neediness, raise your hands, and say: O Allah, O Allah. Whoever does not do that, it is deficient."
"17670","Rawh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id, from Ibn Abi Anas, from 'Abd Allah ibn Nafi' Ibn al-'Amya', from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is two by two; you make tashahhud in every two rak'ahs, show humility and neediness, raise your hands, and say: O Allah, O Allah. Whoever does not do that, it is deficient. Shu'bah said: I said: His prayer is deficient? He said: Yes. I said to him: What is raising? He spread his hands as though supplicating."
